# Hand-written examples against the mock FeatureServer. Start it first (F5 in VS Code, or `npm start`).
# All 70 library requests are in library.http.

@layer = http://127.0.0.1:3000/arcgis/rest/services/ServiceRequests/FeatureServer/0

### Service directory
GET http://127.0.0.1:3000/arcgis/rest/services?f=pjson

### Layer definition (fields, extent, capabilities)
GET {{layer}}?f=pjson

### Ten newest open requests in Khayelitsha, lon/lat output
GET {{layer}}/query?f=pjson&where=Suburb='Khayelitsha' AND Status <> 'Closed'&outFields=RequestID,Category,CategorySub,Status,DtLogged&orderByFields=ObjectID DESC&resultRecordCount=10&outSR=4326

### Same, as GeoJSON
GET {{layer}}/query?f=geojson&where=Suburb='Khayelitsha' AND Status <> 'Closed'&outFields=RequestID,Category,CategorySub,Status&resultRecordCount=10

### Envelope (city centre) in WGS84 — count only
GET {{layer}}/query?f=pjson&geometry=18.40,-33.94,18.45,-33.90&geometryType=esriGeometryEnvelope&inSR=4326&spatialRel=esriSpatialRelIntersects&returnCountOnly=true

### 1.5 km buffer around a point in the city centre
GET {{layer}}/query?f=pjson&geometry=18.4241,-33.9249&geometryType=esriGeometryPoint&inSR=4326&distance=1500&units=esriSRUnit_Meter&outFields=RequestID,Category,Suburb&outSR=4326

### Polygon (Khayelitsha box) — POST with Esri JSON geometry, grouped by Category
POST {{layer}}/query
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

f=pjson
&geometry={"rings":[[[18.64,-34.07],[18.72,-34.07],[18.72,-34.01],[18.64,-34.01],[18.64,-34.07]]],"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326}}
&geometryType=esriGeometryPolygon
&inSR=4326
&groupByFieldsForStatistics=Category
&outStatistics=[{"statisticType":"count","onStatisticField":"ObjectID","outStatisticFieldName":"n"}]
&orderByFields=n DESC

### Median and P90 days to complete by Category (native SQL)
POST {{layer}}/query
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

f=pjson
&where=DtCompleted IS NOT NULL
&sqlFormat=native
&groupByFieldsForStatistics=Category
&outStatistics=[{"statisticType":"percentile_cont","onStatisticField":"DATEDIFF(day, DtLogged, DtCompleted)","statisticParameters":{"value":0.5},"outStatisticFieldName":"MedianDays"},{"statisticType":"percentile_cont","onStatisticField":"DATEDIFF(day, DtLogged, DtCompleted)","statisticParameters":{"value":0.9},"outStatisticFieldName":"P90Days"},{"statisticType":"count","onStatisticField":"ObjectID","outStatisticFieldName":"n"}]
&having=COUNT(ObjectID) > 15
&orderByFields=P90Days DESC

### Time filter (epoch ms) — what the TimeSlider sends: June–August 2026
GET {{layer}}/query?f=pjson&time=1780264800000,1788213599000&returnCountOnly=true

### Pagination
GET {{layer}}/query?f=pjson&where=1=1&outFields=ObjectID,RequestID&orderByFields=ObjectID&resultOffset=100&resultRecordCount=5&returnGeometry=false

### Mock extension: T-SQL against the same data
POST {{layer}}/sql
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

f=pjson
&q=SELECT TOP 5 Suburb, COUNT(*) AS Requests FROM ServiceRequest GROUP BY Suburb ORDER BY Requests DESC
